{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/913812-will-the-subnet-be-back-at-any-point-my-games-are-worse-with-the-lack-of-it","id":913812,"title":"Will the subnet be back at any point? My games are worse with the lack of it.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-13T19:46:36-07:00","id":913812,"title":"Will the subnet be back at any point? My games are worse with the lack of it.","content":"Now the subnet was great, because I don't know everyone's powers, and I don't know what book they're from. The layout wasn't perfect, but it was very, very convenient. I was practically relying on it because, y'know, it's way quicker to find something there than it is in the books.<br /> <br /> Last session I ran we had moments like 'ah, I don't know how that power works, I'll go read the rules on it. <i>Rites of the blood</i> right? Page... let me just find it. Ah, Ok. Here's the section it should be under... hmmm... Oh, yeah, I think this one was in the core book. Give me a minute. Should be just under...&quot; <br /> <br /> My player was literally complaining about how slow the session was. He was right. It was the slowest session of every chronicle I've ever ran. Maybe it's because I'm young and beautiful and haven't had much experience routing through the great tomes, or because my players are using powers I've yet to memorise, but running through blood magic or certain disciplines and especially werewolf gifts has been a lot slower. What was once a 10 second search is now a multi-minute destruction of the game's pacing, and on more than one occasion I've had to be reminded where we were after such a distraction. <br /> <br /> Thing Is I don't get the shutdown. There's no real practical use of it. If I wanted to buy the books I'd buy the books, and if I didn't want to buy the books I wouldn't buy the books. There's no &quot;the subnet is down, Best buy the books&quot; from me. Subnet doesn't prevent sales, It helps them. My players have gone out and bought books because we've had some great games thanks to subnet. Similarly, Subnet being taken down doesn't stop anyone from downloads, filesharing or book borrowing; and it kinda feels like a rude gesture to the fans. I don't see the merit in keeping it down. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7244-innocent-flower","name":"Innocent Flower","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7244_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-13T20:11:04-07:00","id":913824,"title":"","content":"Ok, first of all, don't look stuff up during games. It breaks narrative flow and brings the game to a grinding halt. If you can't be bothered to learn the rules for all the abilities you allow in your games, either restrict the options you allow or get comfortable making rulings on the fly.<br /> <br /> Second of all, what the subnet was doing was illegal. Whether you, or anyone else, is going to buy more books or not now that it's gone is tangential at best to the reason it was shut down. No, it's not coming back, because directly copying and pasting huge sections of text like the subnet did is a violation of copyright and an act of piracy.<br /> <br /> Third of all, <span style=\"color:red\">endorsement or discussion of illegal activities outside the context of game narrative is against the forum rules. This thread will be locked, along with any others like it.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}